- Per-step timeout → blocked (not UNKNOWN). A *model* timeout returns null → blocked. A *pytest* timeout → UNKNOWN per case. A *judge* timeout → blocked. A *verdict* crash → exit 2 → blocked. So: probe/infra timeout -> UNKNOWN only inside matrix; everything else blocks the whole run.

Also: `e3-classify` model null blocks; but if the model writes a `classify.json` with fewer cases (omits cases), verdict gives missing labels default human → UNKNOWN. Good.
- If the classifier writes kind "executable" for a human-only case and no probes, UNKNOWN. Good.
